#
# Token layer image: every colour in the interface becomes a named token.
#
# Second of the three graphics steps the Owner fixed in order (D-0118), after the structure
# and before palette and themes. Nine themes and a free colour picker (UI-020…UI-026) are
# remappings of tokens; until this image there was no layer to remap — 102 distinct colour
# literals were spread through the stylesheet and ten custom properties covered the rest.
#
# What this image changes: 130 literals replaced by 102 named tokens, grouped into surfaces,
# text, accent, semantic state, lines/borders/focus, and shadows/glows. One dead token was
# removed (`--violet`, declared once and referenced nowhere).
#
# ⚠️ What this image does NOT change: anything that is painted.
#
# That is not a claim, it is a measurement. A colour snapshot was taken from a real browser
# BEFORE the refactor and again from these exact bytes: every computed colour property of
# every element across all 25 surfaces — 39,320 elements, 6,133 distinct class signatures.
#
#   colour tuples changed : 0
#   keys that appeared    : 0
#   keys that disappeared : 0
#
# And the snapshot was proved sensitive rather than assumed to be: moving ONE token by one
# unit of blue (#b8c6da -> #b8c6db) moved 29 signatures. A check that cannot fail is not
# evidence.
#
# Why an overlay rather than a rebuild from oci/Dockerfile — unchanged from the reasoning in
# Dockerfile.phase4 through Dockerfile.phase4-structure:
#
#   * oci/Dockerfile runs `apt-get install`, which needs the Debian archives. No network
#     operation is authorised here, and repeating the apt step would silently re-resolve the
#     OS package set to whatever the archive serves today.
#   * Building FROM the audited :phase4-structure image inherits every layer unchanged, so
#     the only difference between the two images is first-party source.
#
# SCHEMA: no change. `AI_STATE_VERSION` is unchanged, and the installed workspace was
# verified to still read `"schemaVersion": 1` immediately before this build. Rolling back to
# :phase4-structure is therefore just starting the old container. A full runtime backup is
# taken with the service stopped regardless.
#
# `services/reference-control-plane/src/` is untouched by this phase and is copied anyway, so
# the deployed artifact is provably the repository tree rather than a partial overlay.
#
# Lineage, stated rather than hidden — now nine deep:
#
#   node:22-bookworm-slim@sha256:6c74791e…
#     -> :phase3 -> :phase4 -> :phase4-complete -> :phase4-complete-lan
#     -> :phase4-webui -> :phase4-wp2 -> :phase4-structure -> :phase4-tokens
#
# Phase 5 packaging should still rebuild from oci/Dockerfile with a recorded network step,
# as D-0033 and D-0053 both say.
#
# Built with --network=none --pull=false.
FROM noesar-evolution:phase4-structure

USER root
COPY --chown=10001:10001 apps/webui-static/ /opt/noesar/apps/webui-static/
COPY --chown=10001:10001 services/reference-control-plane/src/ /opt/noesar/services/reference-control-plane/src/
USER 10001:10001
